.TH AXON-SERVER 1 "2026" "axon-server" "Axon"
.SH NAME
axon-server \- personal Matrix state layer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B axon-server
[\fB--config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.PP
.B axon-server
[\fB--config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.I COMMAND
.SH DESCRIPTION
Axon sits between a Matrix homeserver and clients.
It owns sync, E2EE decryption, search, and a media proxy,
and exposes a versioned HTTP + WebSocket API at /v1/.
.PP
With no command it runs the server.
Every command honors
.B --config
(and otherwise
.IR AXON_CONFIG ,
then
.IR ./axon.toml ,
then the platform config path).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --config " PATH"
Config file.
Overrides
.I AXON_CONFIG
and convention-based discovery.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and build metadata.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Write a starter config (generated
.I store_key
plus the Postgres URL) to the platform config directory,
or to
.B --config
when given.
Refuses to overwrite an existing file unless
.B --force
is passed.
.RS
.TP
.BI --database-url " URL"
Postgres URL to write.
.TP
.B --force
Overwrite an existing config (regenerates
.IR store_key ,
which orphans encrypted data).
.TP
.B --non-interactive
No prompts; flags and defaults only.
.TP
.B --no-token
Do not mint a first bearer token.
.TP
.B --print-token
Mint and print a first bearer token (database must be reachable).
.TP
.B --start-postgres
If the database is down, start a loopback Postgres in Docker.
.TP
.B --tui-config
After minting a token, write it into
.IR ~/.config/axon-tui/config.toml .
.RE
.TP
.B token issue --label \fILABEL\fR
Mint a client bearer token and print the secret once.
.TP
.B token list
List tokens and their status (never prints secrets).
.TP
.B token revoke \fIID\fR | \fB--label\fR \fILABEL\fR
Revoke a token by id or by unique label.
.TP
.B search reindex
Clear the search seed marker so the next server start reseeds the
index from Postgres.
.TP
.B utd redecrypt --account-id \fIID\fR
Retry pending Unable-To-Decrypt back-fill for one account.
Optional
.B --base-url
and
.B --token
(defaults
.I AXON_BASE_URL
/
.IR AXON_TOKEN ,
then
.IR http://127.0.0.1:8080 ).
.TP
.B oauth bind --provider \fINAME\fR
Start binding an upstream OIDC identity (prints a URL to open).
.TP
.B oauth identities list
List bound identities.
.TP
.B oauth identities unbind \fIID\fR
Unbind an identity and revoke tokens it minted.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/axon-server/config.toml
Packaged-install config (generated on first configure when a local
Postgres cluster is reachable).
.TP
.I /var/lib/axon-server
Durable state (SDK store, search index, staged uploads).
.TP
.I /var/cache/axon-server
Disposable media cache.
.SH SEE ALSO
.B axon-server --help
and
.B axon-server \fICOMMAND\fR --help
for flag-level detail.
The source-tree
.I axon.toml.example
is the full config reference.
